# mutgap4_res_mapper_buffer_discard_keeps_mapping: A mapper-ref buffer supports discard: 63 releases its surface but keeps the resource and its mapping ID, so after the guest rewrites the buffer's object record to name mapping 2, the next exec retains surface 1 again and a copy out of the buffer reads surface 1's page, not surface 2's. Surfaces 1 and 2 are mapped over their own pages, each with its own pattern (resources_mapper's _surfaces). Map and isolate only (the IOSurface host device needs a memory map).
